# A step that writes a table and reads it back, and hands on what it read: the read is of the table as `keep` left it,
# inside the step, so the table keeps what `keep` leaves there, in the codomain (rule 4, as `readback-one-body`);
# what was read goes back to the module the `bin` runs, which prints it. The library's operations whose result the
# body names are steps: `const db = new Database(..)`, and `const stored = db.prepare(..).all()`, which `db` goes into
# through the call it runs on; `stored.map(..)`, returned unnamed, is keep's own.

route shortcut.cli
step cli.ts/Ledger()
step cli.ts/Ledger.keep
known #new step cli.ts/Ledger.keep/Database()                   # I
step cli.ts/Ledger.keep/all

line entry > cli.ts call
line cli.ts/Ledger() > Ledger@cli.ts/Ledger() value
line Ledger@cli.ts/Ledger() > cli.ts/Ledger.keep value
line cli.ts/Ledger.keep > Ledger@cli.ts/Ledger.keep value       # keep changes the ledger it runs on (`this.kept +=`)
known #new line cli.ts/Ledger.keep/Database() > _·db@cli.ts/Ledger.keep/Database() value      # I
known #new line Ledger@cli.ts/Ledger() > cli.ts/Ledger.keep/Database() value  # I, K
known #new line _·db@cli.ts/Ledger.keep/Database() > cli.ts/Ledger.keep/all value              # I
known #new line _·db@cli.ts/Ledger.keep/Database() > cli.ts/Ledger.keep value                 # I, then #101
line cli.ts/Ledger.keep/all > _·stored@cli.ts/Ledger.keep/all value
known #101 line _·stored@cli.ts/Ledger.keep/all > cli.ts/Ledger.keep value     # keep maps it and hands it back
line cli.ts/Ledger.keep > SQLite(notes) own
known #new line cli.ts/Ledger.keep > cli.ts back                # the notes read back, a string[], go back (A)
line cli.ts > Screen own

home Ledger@cli.ts/Ledger() cli.ts
home Ledger@cli.ts/Ledger.keep cli.ts
known #new home _·db@cli.ts/Ledger.keep/Database() cli.ts/Ledger.keep                          # I
home _·stored@cli.ts/Ledger.keep/all cli.ts/Ledger.keep

side entry left
side SQLite(notes) right
side Screen right

# A: a step that also changes what it runs on hands its result of no type of the code's back to nothing.
# B: a call into a library whose result the body does not name, and which changes nothing, is drawn as a step:
#    `stored.map(..)` is returned unnamed, so what it gives goes into keep's own result
known #new extra step cli.ts/Ledger.keep/stored.map
known #new extra line _·stored@cli.ts/Ledger.keep/all > cli.ts/Ledger.keep/stored.map value
# I: a library's constructor whose result the body names (`const db = new Database(..)`) is no step, so `db` is no
#    value; `duckdb.connect(..)` and `Connection::open(..)`, which say the same, are steps.
# #101: a value made in the body and used by the body's own calls has no taker
# K: a value handed through a field reaches no step inside: `new Database(this.path)` hands `this` (#121, decision 1,
#    cause 3: the reader's `held_in` skips `this` even inside an argument)
